  "body": "<!-- HELD DRAFT: do not merge. The equivalence proof failed. -->\n\n**Status: HELD. The equivalence proof failed, so this change does not merge.**\n\n## What changed\n\nLaw (c) (`band_reach_counted`) builds the model planes for its island boundary samples from the cut LEVELS plus the deepest cut. The builder is `crates/sim/src/verify/cut_planes.rs`. `Rest::new` is unchanged and still keys a cut per feed chord. No other law changes.\n\nFiles:\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/cut_planes.rs` (new)\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/reach.rs` (call site)\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/rest.rs` (`cut()` accessor is test-only now)\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/reach_tests.rs` (cost assertion; verdict pin unchanged)\n- `crates/sim/src/verify/mod.rs`, `docs/decisions/3615-verify-cut-levels.md`\n\n## The equivalence result (the gate is RED)\n\nThe pin `verify::reach_tests::a_many_plane_ramp_reads_only_the_samples_near_its_discs` fails on the existing sloped ramp fixture `ramp_at(500, 36.0)`.\n\n- All-plane reference (`reach_reference`): `ShankHit { part: true }` at moves 250 to 292 and 293 to 329.\n- New levels plus deepest: `ShankHit { part: true }` at moves 250 to 273 and 293 to 329.\n- Lost: moves 274 to 292. That is 19 part-true convictions.\n\nThe lost moves are real collisions. The shank bottom stands below the boss top Z 10 and its rim reaches 1 mm into the boss wall. The flute did not clear that wall point. The per-chord planes also place triangulation-tie wall vertices at z-dependent positions, and those points catch the moves. One plane cannot reproduce them.\n\nThe other pins pass: `indexed_band_reach_keeps_every_finding_of_the_pooled_scan`, `degenerate_paths_match_the_pooled_scan_and_do_not_panic`, and the three `cut_planes` unit tests.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Away-from-wall ramp `ramp_at(2000, 34)` where verdicts do match: new `slices = 1`, `sample_tests = 0`; old `slices = 2000`, `sample_tests = 32,016,000`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: NOT RUN. Condition 4 says STOP when any verdict differs. A heavy lane cannot recover a lost verdict, so the proof stopped at the pin.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The full heavy sim/verify lanes and the release tier.\n- The real #3577 fig8 path. The counterexample is the existing sloped ramp fixture, and it is enough to stop.\n\n## Why this is held\n\nA verifier change that loses part-true collisions is less conservative. The Prime Directive forbids it. A fix needs a plane set that keeps this wall coverage while it collapses the duplicate planes, for example a bounded set of wall points or samples taken from the mesh edges. That is a new design, not the levels-plus-deepest set.\n\n`docs/decisions/3615-verify-cut-levels.md` has the full record.\n\nChangelog: none (held draft, does not merge)\n\nEffort: high\nRefs #3615\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
